30,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems we are billed by area, not people, and changing power lines costs money every single time we move.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that some areas are much noisier than others, and it takes a long time to get the chairs and desks feeling right.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"The ""free"" style upstairs takes nearly ten minutes every morning, and our past shuffles were a total nightmare of boxes and interruptions.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Interesting. The current plan leaves some people in the dark, and our arrival times are so staggered that ""first-come"" isn't fair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I found that sitting near each other helps us learn and communicate much faster... even the new people benefit from just overhearing us.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, if shuffles are that disruptive, we should avoid any layout that requires frequent movement.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, but if we stay in one spot, some of us might be stuck in the noisy area. That doesn't feel fair.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, but spending ten minutes every morning just to start working sounds like a waste of my gaps.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,Exactly. A free-for-all just rewards the early birds and leaves the rest of us with the interior wall.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If we group by function, maybe we can keep the people who need to talk close together?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, that sounds rational. It also minimizes the need for the expensive power re-runs I discovered.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Minato,,"But what about the chairs? If we move around, we have to spend days adjusting them again.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,That's another point against rotating or free seating. Stability seems better for our focus and our time.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"So we have a conflict between ""fairness"" in location and ""efficiency"" in routine.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just think... we shouldn't lose the chance to help each other by being too spread out.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"Given the budget constraints and the cost of changes, a fixed arrangement seems the most sustainable.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I agree, as long as we carefully choose who sits where so the noise doesn't bother people.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm all for fixed desks. No more boxes, no more morning setup waste.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I can support fixed desks, provided we don't just let the ""usual"" hierarchy decide the window seats.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I think fixed desks by function would help me feel more connected to the team.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
